            <ArticleTitle>Behavioral method for study of pain in the monkey.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>37-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A behavioral method is described in which increasing intensities of electric shocks were applied to the gasserian ganglia of alert monkeys. The animals were trained to press a lever to regulate the shock level. &quot;Pain thresholds&quot; were thereby obtained, and these thresholds were modified by varying the shock duration and by administration of morphine.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
